IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa11-part16-ch2-private`

-- coa11-tests-ch2-private.l4: tests for coa11-part16-ch2-private.l4 (ss 485 to 488).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it, before the run.
-- Argument order is the order of the function's GIVEN.  A #TRACE prints FULFILLED or BREACH and cannot be asserted on
-- the stable binary (a DEONTIC value cannot be compared); the expected outcome of each trace is written beside it and
-- was read off the printed result by hand (NOTES.md, "What the stable binary does not accept").

§ `Tests: Part 16 Chapter 2, private companies`

§§ `s 485(1): an auditor must be appointed for each financial year`

-- arguments: private company, directors resolved no auditor on the ground audited accounts unlikely, resolution reasonable
#ASSERT `s 485(1) an auditor or auditors of the private company must be appointed for the financial year` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485(1) an auditor or auditors of the private company must be appointed for the financial year` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "unless the directors reasonably resolve otherwise"
#ASSERT `s 485(1) an auditor or auditors of the private company must be appointed for the financial year` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- a resolution that is not reasonable does not excuse
#ASSERT `s 485(1) an auditor or auditors of the private company must be appointed for the financial year` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- no resolution
#ASSERT `s 485(1) an auditor or auditors of the private company must be appointed for the financial year` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not a private company: section 489 is the public company rule

§§ `s 485(2): the period for appointing auditors`

#ASSERT `s 485(2) the last day of the 28 days beginning with` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS Date 28 1 2025  -- the first day is day 1 of the 28
#ASSERT `s 485(2) the last day of the 28 days beginning with` (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `s 485(2) the last day of the 28 days beginning with` (Date 5 2 2024) EQUALS Date 3 3 2024  -- across a leap February
#ASSERT `s 485(2) the last day of the 28 days beginning with` (Date 15 9 2025) EQUALS Date 12 10 2025
-- (a) the end of the time allowed (30 September 2025), or (b) if earlier, the day copies are sent out (section 423)
#ASSERT (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) (JUST (Date 15 9 2025)))'s `s 485(2) first day of the period for appointing auditors` EQUALS Date 15 9 2025  -- (b) is earlier: it counts
#ASSERT (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) (JUST (Date 15 9 2025)))'s `s 485(2) last day of the period for appointing auditors` EQUALS Date 12 10 2025
#ASSERT (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) (JUST (Date 5 10 2025)))'s `s 485(2) first day of the period for appointing auditors` EQUALS Date 30 9 2025  -- (b) is later: (a) governs
#ASSERT (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) (JUST (Date 5 10 2025)))'s `s 485(2) last day of the period for appointing auditors` EQUALS Date 27 10 2025
#ASSERT (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) (JUST (Date 30 9 2025)))'s `s 485(2) first day of the period for appointing auditors` EQUALS Date 30 9 2025  -- the same day
#ASSERT (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) NOTHING)'s `s 485(2) first day of the period for appointing auditors` EQUALS Date 30 9 2025  -- copies not yet sent out
#ASSERT (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) NOTHING)'s `s 485(2) last day of the period for appointing auditors` EQUALS Date 27 10 2025
-- the appointment must be made before the end of the period (first 15 September, last 12 October 2025)
#ASSERT `s 485(2) the appointment is made before the end of the period for appointing auditors` FALSE (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) (JUST (Date 15 9 2025))) (Date 12 10 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the last day of the period
#ASSERT `s 485(2) the appointment is made before the end of the period for appointing auditors` FALSE (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) (JUST (Date 15 9 2025))) (Date 13 10 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- one day late
#ASSERT `s 485(2) the appointment is made before the end of the period for appointing auditors` FALSE (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) (JUST (Date 15 9 2025))) (Date 15 9 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the first day
#ASSERT `s 485(2) the appointment is made before the end of the period for appointing auditors` FALSE (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) (JUST (Date 15 9 2025))) (Date 1 9 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- before the period begins: still before its end
#ASSERT `s 485(2) the appointment is made before the end of the period for appointing auditors` TRUE (`s 485(2) the period for appointing auditors` (Date 30 9 2025) (JUST (Date 15 9 2025))) (Date 13 10 2025) EQUALS NOTHING  -- the company's first financial year: not covered

§§ `s 485(3) and (4): who may appoint`

-- s 485(3) arguments: (a) before the first period, (b) after a period of exemption, (c) casual vacancy
#ASSERT `s 485(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not covered: a grant limited by its own wording
-- s 485(4) arguments: (a) during a period, (b) failed during a period, (c) directors failed, section 282 answer
#ASSERT `s 485(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING  -- none of the three occasions
#ASSERT `s 485(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING  -- not an ordinary resolution: the grant is of an appointment by one
#ASSERT `s 485(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING  -- section 282 not known

§§ `s 485(5): only in accordance with this section, section 486 or section 486A`

-- arguments: in accordance with 485, in accordance with 486 or 486A, deemed re-appointment under 487
#ASSERT `s 485(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "may only be appointed"
#ASSERT `s 485(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING  -- a deemed re-appointment: "without prejudice"
#ASSERT `s 485(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 485A: public interest entities with audit committees`

-- s 485A(1),(2) arguments: under 485(4), private, public interest entity, audit committee, Auditor General
#ASSERT `s 485A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "it does not apply to the appointment of an Auditor General"
#ASSERT `s 485A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not a public interest entity: a scope limit, not covered
#ASSERT `s 485A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- no audit committee (section 485B applies instead)
#ASSERT `s 485A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- public interest entity not known
#ASSERT `s 485A(1) the section applies to the appointment` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not an appointment under section 485(4)
#ASSERT `s 485A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not a private company (section 489A is the public company rule)
#ASSERT `s 485A(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- an Auditor General: the flat negative holds whatever else is unknown
-- s 485A(3): the two steps before the appointment (traces: ten days to the appointment)
-- expected: committee recommends on day 3 -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 485A(3)(a) the audit committee must make a recommendation to the directors before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 485A the audit committee` DOES `s 485A(3)(a) make a recommendation to the directors in connection with the appointment` AT 3
-- expected: nothing done by day 11 -> BREACH BY the audit committee
#TRACE `s 485A(3)(a) the audit committee must make a recommendation to the directors before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 11)
-- expected: the directors propose on day 10 (the last day) -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 485A(3)(b) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 485A the directors` DOES `s 485A(3)(b) propose an auditor or auditors for appointment` AT 10
-- expected: the directors act on day 11 -> BREACH BY the directors
#TRACE `s 485A(3)(b) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 485A the directors` DOES `s 485A(3)(b) propose an auditor or auditors for appointment` AT 11
-- the same duties as a decision (arguments: appointment made, committee before, directors before)
#ASSERT `s 485A(3) the audit committee recommended and the directors proposed before the appointment was made` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485A(3) the audit committee recommended and the directors proposed before the appointment was made` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 485A(3) the audit committee recommended and the directors proposed before the appointment was made` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 485A(3) the audit committee recommended and the directors proposed before the appointment was made` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- the appointment has not been made: the time has not run
-- s 485A(4) and (7): arguments: section 485A(1) answer, small or medium sized enterprise, re-appointment recommended and agreed
#ASSERT `s 485A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "unless the company is a small or medium sized enterprise"
#ASSERT `s 485A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- subsection (7): subsections (4) and (5)(a),(b) do not apply
#ASSERT `s 485A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the section does not apply (an Auditor General)
#ASSERT `s 485A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not covered: whether the section applies is not known
#ASSERT `s 485A(4) the audit committee or the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- a small or medium sized enterprise needs no selection procedure whether or not the section applies
-- s 485A(5): arguments: first and second choice, reasons, free from third party influence, no Article 16(6) term, re-appointment agreed
#ASSERT `s 485A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (a) missing
#ASSERT `s 485A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (b) missing
#ASSERT `s 485A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (c)(i) missing
#ASSERT `s 485A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (c)(ii) missing
#ASSERT `s 485A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- subsection (7): (a) and (b) fall away on a re-appointment both agree on
#ASSERT `s 485A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- but (c) still applies
#ASSERT `s 485A(5) the audit committee's recommendation meets the requirements` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 485A(6): arguments: includes the recommendation, departs from the preference, includes candidates drawn from the procedure, includes reasons
#ASSERT `s 485A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- follows the committee: (b) does not bite
#ASSERT `s 485A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- departs: (b)(ii) reasons missing
#ASSERT `s 485A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- departs: (b)(i) recommendation missing
#ASSERT `s 485A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (a) the recommendation not included
#ASSERT `s 485A(6) the directors' proposal meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 485B: public interest entities without audit committees`

#ASSERT `s 485B(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485B(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- an Auditor General
#ASSERT `s 485B(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- the company has an audit committee (section 485A applies instead)
#ASSERT `s 485B(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not a public interest entity
#ASSERT `s 485B(1) the section applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- audit committee not known
#ASSERT `s 485B(1) the section applies to the appointment` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- expected: the directors propose on day 4 -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 485B(3) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 485B the directors` DOES `s 485B(3) propose an auditor or auditors for appointment` AT 4
-- expected: day 11 reached with no proposal -> BREACH BY the directors
#TRACE `s 485B(3) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment before the appointment is made` 10 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 11)
#ASSERT `s 485B(3) the directors proposed an auditor or auditors before the appointment was made` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485B(3) the directors proposed an auditor or auditors before the appointment was made` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 485B(3) the directors proposed an auditor or auditors before the appointment was made` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 485B(4),(5): arguments: section 485B(1) answer, small or medium sized enterprise, proposal is to re-appoint
#ASSERT `s 485B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- small or medium sized enterprise
#ASSERT `s 485B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- subsection (5): a proposal to re-appoint the existing auditor
#ASSERT `s 485B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 485B(4) the directors must carry out a selection procedure in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Audit Regulation` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 485B(4) the proposed auditor or auditors are drawn from the selection procedure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485B(4) the proposed auditor or auditors are drawn from the selection procedure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not drawn from it
#ASSERT `s 485B(4) the proposed auditor or auditors are drawn from the selection procedure` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- no procedure

§§ `s 485C: restriction on appointment of the auditor of a private company which is a public interest entity`

-- the four years begin on the day after the last day of the last financial year of the maximum engagement period
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the first day of the period of 4 years` (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS Date 1 1 2025
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the last day of the period of 4 years` (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS Date 31 12 2028
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the first day of the period of 4 years` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 1 3 2024
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the last day of the period of 4 years` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2028  -- four years beginning 1 March 2024 end on the day before 1 March 2028, which is 29 February 2028 (a leap year)
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the last day of the period of 4 years` (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2029
-- s 485C(1) arguments: private PIE, auditor for every year of the period, last day of the maximum engagement period, first day of the proposed year, Auditor General
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the first day of the four years
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 31 12 2028) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the last day of the four years
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2029) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- a year that begins after the four years
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- a year that begins before the four years
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not auditor for every year of the period
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not a public interest entity
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` NOTHING TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- public interest entity not known
#ASSERT `s 485C(1) the person is barred from appointment as auditor of the company for the financial year` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- subsection (3): an Auditor General
-- s 485C(2) arguments: private PIE, the auditor of subsection (1) was auditor for every year, the person is of the same network, dates, Auditor General
#ASSERT `s 485C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 485C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2029) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- outside the four years
#ASSERT `s 485C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not of that network
#ASSERT `s 485C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the auditor mentioned in (1) was not in that position
#ASSERT `s 485C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not a public interest entity
#ASSERT `s 485C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` NOTHING TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 485C(2) the person is barred as a member of the same network as the auditor mentioned in subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- an Auditor General

§§ `s 486: default power of the Secretary of State`

#ASSERT `s 486(1) the Secretary of State may appoint one or more persons to fill the vacancy` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486(1) the Secretary of State may appoint one or more persons to fill the vacancy` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- no failure: the power is not given; not covered
-- s 486(2) arguments: section 485(2) applies, the company fails to make the necessary appointment
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the company must give the Secretary of State notice that his power has become exercisable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the company must give the Secretary of State notice that his power has become exercisable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- it made the appointment in time
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the company must give the Secretary of State notice that his power has become exercisable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the company's first financial year: subsection (2) of section 485 does not apply
-- the period for appointing auditors ended on 12 October 2025: one week runs to 19 October 2025
-- arguments: last day of the period, the day the notice was given, the day now
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the period for appointing auditors` (Date 12 10 2025) (JUST (Date 19 10 2025)) (Date 30 10 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- the seventh day after the end
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the period for appointing auditors` (Date 12 10 2025) (JUST (Date 20 10 2025)) (Date 30 10 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the eighth day
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the period for appointing auditors` (Date 12 10 2025) (JUST (Date 13 10 2025)) (Date 30 10 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the period for appointing auditors` (Date 12 10 2025) NOTHING (Date 19 10 2025) EQUALS NOTHING  -- no notice yet and the week has not run
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the company gave the notice within one week of the end of the period for appointing auditors` (Date 12 10 2025) NOTHING (Date 20 10 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- no notice and the week has run
-- the duty as a regulative rule (day 0 is the end of the period): expected FULFILLED, BREACH, BREACH
#TRACE `s 486(2) the company must give notice to the Secretary of State within one week of the end of the period for appointing auditors` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 486(2) give notice to the Secretary of State of his power having become exercisable` AT 7
#TRACE `s 486(2) the company must give notice to the Secretary of State within one week of the end of the period for appointing auditors` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 486(2) give notice to the Secretary of State of his power having become exercisable` AT 8
#TRACE `s 486(2) the company must give notice to the Secretary of State within one week of the end of the period for appointing auditors` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 8)
-- the offence: arguments: the company failed to give the notice
#ASSERT `s 486(3)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486(3)(a) the company commits an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not an officer in default
#ASSERT `s 486(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the company gave the notice
#ASSERT `s 486(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING  -- section 1121 not known
-- the penalty: summary conviction only, level 3 and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 3, no imprisonment
#ASSERT `s 486(4) the penalty for an offence under section 486` EQUALS Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
-- pounds: the amount of level 3 is an input (an arbitrary 1000 is used here to show the arithmetic)
#ASSERT `s 486(4) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 486(4) the most the person can be fined for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS 100

§§ `s 486A: defective appointments`

#ASSERT `s 486A(1) the Secretary of State may appoint another auditor or auditors in place of the auditor or auditors appointed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486A(1) the Secretary of State may appoint another auditor or auditors in place of the auditor or auditors appointed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- no breach: the power is not given
#ASSERT `s 486A(1) the Secretary of State may appoint another auditor or auditors in place of the auditor or auditors appointed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486A(2) the breach invalidates the report` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "does not invalidate any report"
#ASSERT `s 486A(2) the breach invalidates the report` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- another report: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 486A(3) sections 1248 and 1249 apply as if the auditor was not an appropriate person for the period during which the audit was conducted` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486A(3) sections 1248 and 1249 apply as if the auditor was not an appropriate person for the period during which the audit was conducted` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- a breach of section 485A or 485B only
-- s 486A(4): the company became aware on 1 March 2025: one week runs to 8 March 2025
-- arguments: the day the company became aware, the day the notice was given, the day now
#ASSERT `s 486A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` (JUST (Date 1 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 31 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` (JUST (Date 1 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 9 3 2025)) (Date 31 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` (JUST (Date 1 3 2025)) NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` (JUST (Date 1 3 2025)) NOTHING (Date 9 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486A(4) the company gave the notice within one week of becoming aware of the breach` NOTHING NOTHING (Date 9 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING  -- the company is not yet aware
-- expected: FULFILLED (day 7), BREACH (day 8)
#TRACE `s 486A(4) the company must give notice to the Secretary of State within one week of becoming aware of the breach` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 486A(4) give notice to the Secretary of State that the power under subsection (1) has become exercisable` AT 7
#TRACE `s 486A(4) the company must give notice to the Secretary of State within one week of becoming aware of the breach` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 486A(4) give notice to the Secretary of State that the power under subsection (1) has become exercisable` AT 8
