§§ `s 487: term of office`

#ASSERT `s 487(1)(a) the auditor or auditors cannot yet take office` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- a previous auditor still holds office
#ASSERT `s 487(1)(a) the auditor or auditors cannot yet take office` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- they have ceased: the bar is over
-- s 487(1)(b) arguments: the day now, the last day of the next period for appointing auditors (12 October 2025), re-appointed
#ASSERT `s 487(1)(b) the auditor or auditors have ceased to hold office` (Date 12 10 2025) (Date 12 10 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- the last day of the period: they still hold office
#ASSERT `s 487(1)(b) the auditor or auditors have ceased to hold office` (Date 13 10 2025) (Date 12 10 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- after the end of the period
#ASSERT `s 487(1)(b) the auditor or auditors have ceased to hold office` (Date 13 10 2025) (Date 12 10 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "unless re-appointed"
#ASSERT `s 487(1)(b) the auditor or auditors have ceased to hold office` (Date 1 10 2025) (Date 12 10 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- before the end of the period
-- s 487(2) arguments: no auditor appointed by the end, an auditor was in office, (a) appointed by the directors, (b) articles require actual re-appointment, (c) section 488 answer, (d) members resolved not, (e) directors resolved none, (f) section 485C
